This is an independent implementation of a network protocol, produced by
analysing how an existing client program communicates, for the purpose of
interoperability. It contains no code, artwork, audio or text taken from
KONAMI's software. It does contain one small table of integers -- the
targets of the scenario branches this server has to arbitrate -- read
mechanically out of the client's data files, because a server cannot
decide those branches without them. It carries no text or imagery and is
meaningless without a lawfully obtained copy of the game. Message names,
map names and structure offsets appear here because they are the
identifiers the protocol itself uses.

